    "narrative": "This Suspicious Activity Report is filed regarding unauthorized financial transactions conducted on payment card C10434-K1, issued to customer C10434 (Investigation ID: HHG-010). Beginning on or about 2016-12-02 at approximately 18:18:27 UTC, the subject account sustained an unauthorized fraud episode totaling $1,000.03 USD across 1 transaction(s) (Transaction IDs: 3506725). The suspicious activity was initiated through an electronic digital channel originating from an unrecognized device profile characterized as 'Windows | Windows 10 | edge 16.0 | 1366x768'. The compromise was conducted as card-not-present fraud using stolen payment card credentials transacted through a hardware device registered as newly seen for this customer account. The total confirmed financial exposure of $1,000.03 USD meets or exceeds the mandatory regulatory threshold of $1,000.00 USD for suspicious activity reporting. Upon out-of-band security contact, the cardholder explicitly denied authorizing or benefiting from the transactions and confirmed continuous physical possession of the original payment card, verifying that electronic card data was intercepted or compromised without authorization. In accordance with Fraud Policy v1.0 and regulatory guidance, payment card C10434-K1 was immediately placed under block status to prevent further losses, and full reimbursement procedures have been initiated for customer C10434. The institution maintains all underlying transaction records, audit logs, and graph relationship artifacts available for law enforcement inspection under reference HHG-010.",
